# Exclusion rules, gitignore style, matched against `repo/path/inside/repo`:
#   **  crosses directories      *  does not cross /      ?  one character
#   a trailing / means a directory (dir/**)
#   a pattern without / matches a file name at any depth
# `idx ignore` shows which files each rule hits. The list is published with the index (meta "ignore"), so a
# search that finds nothing can tell the agent "this path is excluded, look in the local checkout".
#
# Excluded files never reach the database. Anything that is indexed can be read by every client of the
# database: keep secrets, credentials and personal data out with rules here.

notes/private/
notes/.obsidian/
notes/.trash/

**/secrets/
**/*.env
**/node_modules/
**/.git/
